Original synthetic teaching prescriptions, glass coefficients, and aperture
icon are distributed under Apache-2.0 with this project. They do not represent
commercial glass products or production lens designs.

RayOptics is used solely as a development-time independent reference and is
not bundled as the optical engine. See docs/validation-rayoptics.json for the
scope of comparison. Third-party software retains its original license.

The additional real SCHOTT glass catalog is a subset of the CC0-1.0
refractiveindex.info database by Mikhail Polyanskiy, with original data
references to the SCHOTT catalog 2017-01-20b. This subset is not original OSS
teaching data. Pinned provenance and checksums: src/data/glass-catalog.json.
License: glass-catalog-CC0-1.0.txt (docs/catalog/CC0-1.0.txt in source).
M. N. Polyanskiy, Scientific Data 11, 94 (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02898-2

PDF export uses PDF-LIB and @pdf-lib/fontkit (MIT). The fontkit fork lists
Andrew Dillon and original contributor Devon Govett in its package metadata.
Their license declarations and attribution are retained in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.
Noto Sans SC is distributed under SIL OFL 1.1; a regular-weight static instance
is bundled for offline Chinese PDF export. Source checksums and the applied
weight conversion are recorded in src/assets/fonts/source.json and fonts/
in the installation resources. Its OFL text is distributed alongside it.

The unmodified MPL-2.0 selectors component is available in source form at
https://crates.io/crates/selectors/0.38.0 and
https://github.com/servo/stylo/tree/572ecba2d1600e7c3d490586692a209faf703baa/selectors
Supplemental upstream license texts are in docs/licenses/ (source) and are
incorporated into THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt in the installation resources.

Other unmodified MPL-2.0 components are cssparser 0.37.0,
cssparser-macros 0.7.1, dtoa-short 0.3.5, and option-ext 0.2.0.
Their unmodified source is available at:
https://crates.io/crates/cssparser/0.37.0
